<title>CROATIA: Croatia appoints M. Lynch, UBS as rating advisers.</title>
<headline>Croatia appoints M. Lynch, UBS as rating advisers.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia has appointed Merril Lynch and Union Bank of Switzerland as advisers in obtaining credit rating from international rating agencies, the finance ministry said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is expected that the Republic of Croatia will undertake a Eurobond financing shortly after ratings have been obtained, with UBS Ltd and Merril Lynch International as lead managers,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Croatia is hpoing for an investment grade rating of BBB for its maiden issue of Eurobonds, planned at about $150 million.</p>
<p>The statement said the country would approach Standard and Poor's, Moody's Investment service and IBCA for the rating. -- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
